body: "The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n\n- Failing job: `release`\n- Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/35838537739\n- Commit: ccc7765700cc624977a8294adc73c229e83c69d5\n- Date (UTC): 2026-09-23T08:53:58Z\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-09-25T07:52:12Z)\n>\n> Resolved by hand on 2026-09-25. Run 35838537739 published pm-csv@2026.9.23 to npm with a provenance attestation (gitHead 3002a93 = tag v2026.09.23) and pushed the tag, then bun's registry mirror still answered \"No version matching 2026.9.23\" after 8 attempts (4 minutes), so the job failed before creating the GitHub Release. Verified today: `bun add pm-csv@2026.9.23` resolves, and the Release now exists: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/releases/tag/v2026.09.23 (notes list the four dependency bumps in the tag window; no pm items closed in it). The durable fix (10-minute bun window, Release no longer gated on bun, visible gate step) is already on 12 fleet repos and lands here in the 2026-09-25 wave PR; tracking pm-cli-website-3y5d in the companion hub."
